            <ArticleTitle>[Correlation the laevocardiogram and plain chest films in the presence of myocardial insufficiency (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A correlation was attempted in 106 patients with myocardial insufficiency between linear and volume parameters of the laevocardiogram and the corresponding parameters on plain chest films, as well as between pressure measurements and the degree of pulmonary congestion. Measurements on the plain radiograph provide only limited information on the function of the myocardium and the severity of myocardial lesion respectively. Nevertheless, they are of some value during the course of the disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
